# Reproduction only for inc-aiw5; no game-code or data changes.
# Run from repository root, with a fresh INCURSION_RUN_DIR under logs/:
# INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/inc-aiw5/acid" \
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/caustic-vitae-acid.keys 1
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. Caustic Vitae (lib/pspells.irh:1371) promises
# "1d8 points of acid damage per cast level" and "half of the damage dealt
# cannot be resisted". The entity sets no xval, so src/Magic.cpp:560 reads its
# damage type as 0 = AD_NORM, and the EF_HALF_UNTYPED split at src/Effects.cpp
# sends BOTH halves as AD_NORM. An acid-immune victim therefore takes the full
# damage; with the fix it should take only the unresistible half.
#
# ROUTE. Caustic Vitae is an Effect, not a Spell, so it never appears in a
# Learn Spells checklist -- but "Learn Any Spell" (src/Debug.cpp:850) types a
# name and accepts any T_TEFFECT, which this is. A level-2 orc mage is made by
# chargen-mage.keys; Free Advancement buys one level, Infinite Mana makes the
# cast free, and Freeze Monsters stops the victim acting on its own.
#
# TARGET. A magma creeper (lib/mon3.irh:2833, MA_JELLY, HD 12, Con 22) carries
# "Immune: OOZE_IMMUNITIES, DF_FIRE, DF_ACID, DF_ELEC", so it is acid-immune.
# Its hit points are never below 84 whatever the roll (12 HD at 1 each + 12 x
# the Con 22 modifier of 6), far above the 10 that one half can take, so it
# survives and its HP stays readable. It is summoned one square east; the bolt
# is fired east with D RIGHT and the attack roll is forced to 20.
#
# ORACLE. (1) The victim's own HP line in "Examine Nearby Things" (wizard menu
# item 1), read before and after the cast: the summoned monster is the first
# T_MONSTER after the player; Genocide leaves corpses ahead of it, so the
# script presses RIGHT until the header names T_MONSTER. (2) The game's own combat
# numbers, printed to the message history ('v'): before the fix both halves
# read "Physical Damage" and sum to the full amount; after the fix the second
# half is "Acid Damage" and the acid-immune victim is unaffected by it.
# The character is LOADED, not generated (INCURSION_LOAD, set by
# tools/check_caustic_vitae_acid.sh): tools/fixtures/chars/orc-mage-seed1-opt0822.sav,
# the male orc mage chargen-mage.keys builds, WIS 16 (mod +3). Nothing here
# reads a rolled attribute.
@until "Things in View" ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*2 SPACE   # Free Advancement
DOWN*5 SPACE   # Infinite Mana
DOWN*3 SPACE   # Freeze Monsters
ESC

# One level: effective caster level 2, so the damage is 2d8 + Wis mod (3).
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
SPACE
@dump:state

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Caustic Vitae"
ENTER
@dump:learned

# Clear the level first, so the summoned monster is the only other thing the
# Examine screen can reach in one RIGHT, whatever the level holds.
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
SPACE*40                 # dismiss the genocide message chain

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "magma creeper"
RIGHT*4 ENTER
@dump:summoned

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@dump:target-before-player
@until "T_MONSTER" RIGHT   # skip the corpses Genocide left; the victim is the one monster
@dump:target-before
ESC

m
@choose "Caustic Vitae"
D
RIGHT
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after
v
@dump:messages
ESC

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@dump:target-after-player
@until "T_MONSTER" RIGHT   # skip the corpses Genocide left; the victim is the one monster
@dump:target-after
ESC

@quit
